{
 "id": "298-39",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "It's the standard we use here, and it'll ensure you're aligned with the rest of the team.",
  "I'll make sure to guide you through the process, and feel free to reach out anytime you have questions or concerns.",
  "Now, regarding your ongoing project, remember to maintain consistency in your code formatting.",
  "From now on, I want you to end function names with '_x' and attribute names with '_i'.",
  "This will help ensure uniformity and make your code more readable and understandable for your colleagues.",
  "Consistency in coding style makes collaboration much easier and enhances the maintainability of our software projects.",
  "If you have any questions or concerns about this or any other aspect of your project, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "That's what mentorship is all about\u2014supporting each other and sharing knowledge.",
  "It helps us generate and store unique, complex passwords for all our accounts.",
  "From now on, I'd like you to end all attribute names with '_q'.",
  "This change will help us easily identify attributes and maintain a clear distinction from function names.",
  "Consistency across our codebases is important for collaboration and maintenance.",
  "Now, similarly, I'd like you to start ending all function names with '_b'.",
  "This will provide a clear visual cue and help us identify functions at a glance.",
  "For now, just start with any new functions you create, and we can discuss renaming existing functions in our next meeting.",
  "It's a gradual process, and I don't want you to spend too much time on refactoring just yet.",
  "Remember, these standards are important for our team's efficiency and collaboration."
 ],
